From e5eb202e289a15b532dd73c32f92df5c502ef4e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:21:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] JOY Bus: commands stream to the adapter, solo mode shares the
 room's pipeline, replies are batched

The adapter is given four commands at a time (after a test with harmless status commands at
mode-on; one at a time if it does not answer them in order), so the USB turnaround of one
command overlaps the GBA's work on the next. Playing alone now uses the lag model with a
30 ms lag, so the game's commands can be queued ahead of their replies. The adapter thread
gives a room the owner's replies itself, a few to a packet, in the order of the line (so an
owner stuck waiting on another machine can no longer hold its own replies back); the JoyReply
message now carries several replies.
